{"content":[{"c":["EN-ROGEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Spring that was an important landmark identifying the boundary line between the tribes of Judah and Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.7","r":"Josh.15.7","rawR":"Josh.15.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.7","value":"Josh.15.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.16","r":"Josh.18.16","rawR":"Josh.18.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.16","value":"Josh.18.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:16"},"). Jonathan and Ahimaaz hid at En-rogel when they were spying on Absalom’s troops for King David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.17.17","r":"2Sam.17.17","rawR":"2Sam.17.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.17.17","value":"2Sam.17.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 17:17"},"), and from there a maidservant delivered their messages to the king. Here also Adonijah sacrificed sheep, oxen, and goats when he anticipated David’s death and wished to set himself up as king (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.9","r":"1Kgs.1.9","rawR":"1Kgs.1.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.9","value":"1Kgs.1.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Of the two suggested locations for En-rogel, the older suggestion identifies it with a spring in a cave near Siloam, on the west side of the Kidron Valley, known as the Virgin’s Fount. There is strong evidence, however, that this is actually the Gihon Spring (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.33","r":"1Kgs.1.33","rawR":"1Kgs.1.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.33","value":"1Kgs.1.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:33"},"), which is mentioned as distinct from En-rogel. A more likely suggestion is another spring south of Jerusalem known as the Well of Job."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"EnRogel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.7"},{"anchorText":"18:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.16","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.16","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.16"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 17:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.17.17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.17.17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.17.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 1:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.1.9","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.1.9","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.1.9"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 1:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.1.33","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.1.33","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.1.33"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ff9b789359853005fe708d8c01bc7e7ed18b66fed99964d066b645145c1dfc93","sourceItemName":"EnRogel","sourceItemOrder":182,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"EnRogel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"En-Rogel","title":"En-Rogel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}